{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3654","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3654","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3654\",\"parent_revision\":\"431de222ab4bdf36ce5feda95b1b1d8328b36e4565cdbf0ec94ea168912a5556\",\"root_revision\":\"431de222ab4bdf36ce5feda95b1b1d8328b36e4565cdbf0ec94ea168912a5556\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-09-19\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nA `backlog_groom(selector=..., section=..., entry_id=..., content=...)` call that replaces an existing entry can report success while the entry keeps its old content.\\n\\nObserved on #3060, 2026-09-19: the classifier replaced Issue Classification entry 2026-09-19T09:58:32.700806Z and Root-Cause Analysis entry 2026-09-19T10:04:10.796556Z by entry_id. A live `backlog_view(..., refresh=True)` afterwards showed both entries unchanged. `backlog_strike_entry` on the same entries then reported that they do not exist, while `backlog_view` showed them. `sync_status` at that time reported `pending_mutations: 7`, `rejected_mutations: 63`. An earlier entry_id replacement by the fact-checker on the same item, the same day, did take effect. `replace_section=True` writes on the same item took effect.\\n\\nNo tool shows which queued or rejected mutations belong to which call, so a caller cannot tell whether its write is pending, rejected, or applied.\\n\\nImpact: agents believe a correction is in place when the item still carries the wrong content; the workaround (append a new entry that names the one it supersedes) leaves the wrong entry active.\\n\\n**Hypothesis**: entry_id replacement is queued as a pending mutation that is later rejected, and the tool response reflects the local write rather than the backend result.\\n\\nExpected: a replacement either takes effect and reads back, or returns an error; a caller can see the state of its own queued write.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation, re-groom of #3060, 2026-09-19\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-19\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"0f9ff8ca8fa6a7fc0f9d8461c689a404c0f4616fe1516e2d40c3da18901cd106\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVoHvbA\"}"}